In Lounsko a transformer with a value of tens of millions of kroner burns
The blaze has caught in the morning a transformer of the Eeps company in a switch box near the village of Vikov in Lounsko.
According to Luká Marvan, the spokesman for the firefighters of the Urtí region, the fire is extinguished by six groups.
Firefighters previously wanted to let the transformer be destroyed by the blaze, however they later changed their minds and the blaze is extinct it with a mixture of water, foam and special extinguishing material.
The blaze was caused by a technical defect, the transformer short-circuit.
There were none injured, according to Pavla Mandátová, the company's spokeswoman, did not endanger the safe operation of the distribution system.
The estimated damage is several million kroner, listing it exactly won't be possible before the blaze goes out.
According to Mandátova it will be necessary to replace the destroyed transformer with a new one.
During the ten-years of Eeps' activity, nothing similar happened, the breakdowns of this type are sporadic, he added.
According to Sona Holingerová Hendrychová, the spokeswowoman for the company EZ for the northern Czech, the supplies of the electric current were not severed, and the fire of the electric substation did not affect the operation of homes, offices or companies.
In the territory of the Czech Republic as an exclusive maintainer of the distributive system of 400 kV and 220 kV.
It retains in good condition, renovates and develops 39 switch boxes with 67 transformers, which carry the electrical energy of the transmission system to the distributor system, in addition it maintains the electric conduction of 4339 kilometers long.
