World's desolest panorama
The Arctic is changing faster and more dramatically than any other habitat on the planet.
Defining ice is melting at an alarming rate, taking with it the life it can't survive anywhere else.
The interests of oil, gas, transportation and fishing have been focused on newly opened waters, with diplomats, lawyers and now authors, as a result.
