Ironistically, it's in the waters to the north of those two hunting nations that the ice will last for longer.
In his new book, "After the Ice"), Alun Anderson, a former editor of New Scientist, offers a clear and chilling tale of Arctic science and an overwhelming glimpsing gaze on how the future of that place can be transformed.
It isn't that the scientists have every answer.
