U.N. top envoy in Kabul about to resign
U.N. en U.N. envoy Kai Eide said on Friday he would relinquish his post in March, ending a tumultuous tenure that was hurt by allegations of widespread corruption in Afghanistan's U.N.-backed presidential election.
Eide's departure takes place when the Obama administration has decided to send an additional 30,000 U.S. troops to Afghanistan.
