Massive climate mobilisation in Copenhagen and around the world
Dozens of thousands of protesters protested this Saturday in demand of an ambitious and binding agreement to combat global warming, around the world and in Copenhagen, where the police arrested several hundred people.
Some thirty thousand people, according to the police; hundreds of thousands, according to the organizers, paraded for the frosty Danish capital in demand of an agreement that the United Nations Conference on climate change must reach no later than Friday. It would enter into force on 1 January 2013.
For Connie Hedegaard, the Danish president of the Climate Conference, the growing mobilisation of the climate around the world, represented by these demonstrations, contributed to "the political price" of failure in Copenhagen being very high.
