Analysts, on the contrary, expected a deepening of the deficit.
Both imports and exports increased.
The great novelty is the growth of trade volumes, in particular exports of goods, which reflect the growth of the major economies trading with the U.S., said Christopher Cornell of research firm Economy.com.
Renter last week, unemployment enrollments in the U.S. unexpectedly increased, 474,000 applications were filed.
But over the past four weeks, the average number of new job seekers "has been the lowest for a year," said Scott Marcouiller of Wells Fargo Advisors.
The bond market fell.
