Cuba: more than a hundred pro-powered supporters boo "Ladies of White"
Thirteen supporters of Cuban power booed the handcuffs of political prisoners gathered in Havana for the World's Day of Human Rights and prevented another demonstration to which a dozen dissident dissidents were summoned.
Some forty "Ladies of Blanco," wives or relatives of political prisoners, were attacked in the street by supporters of Raúl Castro's government while walking towards the center of the capital demanding the release of these detainees, an AFP journalist said.
"Mercenarias," "The street belongs to the revolutionaries," "Viva Fidel and Raúl" shouted the dissidents with their fist.
The latter were escorted by plainclogued officers who came to "protect them."
On the eve, a similar demonstration unleashed against the "Ladies of Blanco" in Havana, without injuries or arrests.
