Eviction represented an "unacceptable attack" on freedom of research and learning.
The exclusive focus on vandalism served "delegitimization and criminalization of the protest" and diverted the attention of the content.
The governing board has refused to enter into the necessary negotiations.
Teachers demand the immediate withdrawal of the judicial complaint.
Most occupants have caused no material damage, it is said.
legitimized protest
The young people of the Verdi syndicate and the German Federation of Trade Unions are also in solidarity with the students.
The outpouring is the legitimate expression of a growing concern for the future itself, says Verdi's national youth secretary, Alexander Klein.
"CDU), Minister of Sciences of Hessen (CDU), defended, however, the performance of the rector of the university and of the police.
We're thankful to the university's rector.
"Destructism and occupancy are totally unacceptable means," he said at an Aktuelle Stunde broadcast on Thursday in Wiesbaden province.
"We're sympathetic to the protest, but we're not sympathetic to vandalism," said Peter Beuth, a provincial parliament delegate for the CDU.
The opinion of the opposition factions, the SPD, the Greens and the left, is different.
