Instead of thoroughly studying the arguments and demands of the students, they are evicted.
The Left has tabled a motion, requesting the Minister of the Interior to submit a report on police intervention.
Nuevo Silicon Valley
For many years, it was seen as a secret, inaccessible city for Western visitors.
Selenogre, one of Moscow's ten districts, was a heavily guarded site in the Soviet Union for the secret weapons investigation.
Today, the 216,000-strong community, located 37 kilometers from the center of Moscow, is regarded as "Silicon Valley."
Here you will find important micro and nanoelectronic research and production centers.
Already since September 2008, representatives of Selenogre have contacted Riedberg's science headquarters in Frankfurt, the university institutes and companies of the Frankfurt Innovation Centre (FIZ).
Various mutual visits took place and now, on Wednesday, Selenograd and Riedberg signed a "transition of close collaboration protocol" in Frankfurt.
Moscow Deputy Mayor Juri Rosljak and Selen Mayor Anatoly Smirnov spearheaded the Russian delegation; by Frankfurt he signed planning services chief Edwin Schwarz.
In 2010, representatives of FIZ and directors of small and medium-sized enterprises from the natural sciences research centre will travel to a seminar in Selenogre.
Scientist exchange
It's an ongoing scientific exchange.
But it also addresses business relationships.
The FIZ company will have the chance to set foot in the growing Russian market.
In return the Russian scientific companies want to have access to contracts in Germany.
