Endesa and Barcelona, with the electric car
The electricity company Endesa, together with the Barcelona City Council, has created the 'LIVE Office'.
It is a project to develop and promote the electric vehicle in the Catalan capital.
The 'LIVE Office' (Logistics for the Implantation of the Electrical Vehicle) will define and coordinate the road map for the implementation of the electric car in the city and will reach agreements on mobility, managing, coordinating, presenting subsidies, etc.
On the other hand he will develop the MOVELE project, promote the electric car, gather the opinion and work of the sectors involved.
Ultimately, it is intended to promote the transport of the future.
3 'Electrical cities'
But Barcelona isn't the only city that's going to be involved in the implementation of the electric car in Spain.
Madrid and Sevilla join the project.
These are the three cities chosen by the Government, within the MOVELE Plan, to promote the implementation of the electric vehicle.
The electricity company Endesa has already signed a framework agreement with the Generalitat of Catalonia.
This aims to promote research and technological development activities in the Autonomous Community of Catalonia.
These would include activities related to energy and in particular energy efficiency.
It is not the only initiative in which Endesa participates in the promotion of the electric vehicle.
The company participates in standardization groups at European level and has assets a series of complementary projects such as G4V, ELVIRE or CENIT VERDE.
Zapatero sees 'a horizon of tranquillity' for the motor sector
The president of the government, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, glimpses "a horizon of tranquillity" for the Spanish automotive industry, which, he recalled, is the country's main export sector.
In the presentation of the Economic Report of the President of the Government for 2009, Zapatero reviewed the measures the Executive has put in place throughout the exercise to support the automotive sector.
"Without the Automotive Competitivity Plan, today we would have a panorama of abandonment, of closing some of our main production plants," said the president of the government.
"Thanks to this plan and at the disposal of the brands to follow in Spain, in a very competitive sector, we can have a horizon of tranquillity for the future of this industry, which is our main export sector," he added.
In this regard, he recalled that the Competitiveness Plan, included in the Comprehensive Automotive Plan (IPA), allocated 800 million to projects of 19 manufacturers and 137 auxiliary companies, which mobilized an investment of more than 3 billion euros.
The Head of the Executive explained that this investment was committed both to the development of new models and to modernize existing products and processes.
Zapatero also emphasized government measures to support the demand, in reference to Plan 2000E, implemented in collaboration with the Autonomous Communities and automotive brands.
According to the president, this plan has made it possible to reduce by 6% the average emissions of new vehicles marketed on the Spanish market and has led to a "strong increase" in registrations, which grew "40 per cent" in November.
20,000 square meters of classic vehicles
The first edition of the International Classical Eve Exhibition will be celebrated in Madrid, a meeting place space for professionals and amateurs of the world of the engine.
This initiative will be carried out from 5 to 7 February 2010 in the Crystal Pavilion of the Casa de Campo in Madrid.
It is an exhibition area of 20,000 square meters in which there will be more than 200 national and international exhibitors.
Not only you will be able to find classic motorcycles and cars, but in ClassicAuto Madrid you will find items of all kinds related to the engine world.
Thus, among the exhibitors of the pavilion, you can find accessories, spare parts, components, textile accessories, accessories, publications, thumbnails, etc.
Hundreds of articles related to the classic-agine world that will delight collectors and curious.
Participating companies will include, among others, Classics of Mos and Good Old Times, sales of cars; Juan Lumbreras, restoration; Coupe-Francisco Pueche sale and restoration of cars; or Cochera Clásicos, specialist Mercedes Benz.
Skill Tests on the Outdoors
In addition, the commercial activity of this Salon will be completed with parallel activities: holding rallies, sporting exhibitions, skill tests, presentations and competitions.
Skill tests will also be carried out with classic cars and motorbikes on a circuit enabled outside the fairground.
Mazda3 i-Stop
Mazda wants to show that sportsmanship is not at odds with respect for the environment.
For this reason, it has just added to the Mazda3 the stop-and-boot system of the engine (boasted as i-Stop), a device that at least for the time being is only available with the 2.0 gasoline engine with 150 horsepower.
This second-generation Mazda3 stands out for the good note reached in its entirety.
Finishes, vehicle completion, habitability, behavior, mechanics, i-Stop system...
All of these aspects are outstanding in the new Mazda3.
Beginning at the driving post, we see that the front seats have excellent ergonomics and clamping.
Likewise, the touch of the steering wheel is exquisite.
Continuing with the ensemble made up of the instrument painting and the console we see how Mazda has continued the Japanese tendency to create a futuristic interior design, with a large number of buttons and flashy controls and colors in red and blue.
This styling reminds us, in part, of the Honda Civic.
Therefore, we can say that both the Mazda3 and the Civic, both Japanese, stand in contrast to the sobriety of the German products, and more specifically the Volkswagen Golf, to which everyone wants to beat.
Continuing the cottage, this Japanese compact has more than enough habitability for four adults to travel with a high level of comfort.
To all this is a wide trunk and with regular forms.
The automatic stop-and-start system of the engine, at least for the time being, is only available with the gasoline engine of two liters and 150 horsepower and with the manual change of six gears.
This engine is a real delight. It stands out for its finesse, because of its reduced rustory, for the performances and for achieving contained consumption.
Although the most in-mandated Mazda3 will be the diesel versions, those who do not carry out a large number of kilometers a year should not rule out this i-Stop with a gasoline engine, both because of its high running comfort, and because of its contained consumption.
With regard to the level of equipment, the version chosen for the test is the so-called Sportive, i.e. the one that incorporates a greater number of serial elements.
From the standard equipment stands out especially the lane-changing wizard (RVM) that eliminates the dead angle, traction and stability controls, speed control, photosensitive indoor spectacle, the on-board computer on an over-sized screen, parking sensors, stand-alone air-conditioner, rain and light sensor, bluetooth and 17-inch alloy tires.
In addition, in the absence of its equipment, this version had the Premium Pack, which it adds for 1,500 euros: adaptive beacons bixenon and BOSE sound system with disk charger, among other elements.
Conclusion
Mazda3 2.0 i-Stop is one of the best albums in the category.
It stands out especially because of the quality of the materials used, because of their behavior and the high level of equipment.
In addition, those who don't do many kilometers a year will be able to opt for this i-Stop version, associated only with the 150-horseweight 2.0 gasoline engine.
The only inconvenience of this model is its high price, which is between 21,770 euros of the Luxury finish and 23,270 euros of the proven version -Sportive.
In exchange for this lofty figure, the Mazda3 will give us every day great doses of satisfaction.
