About Albert Camus
About Samuel Beckett: "Nihilista, an allegorical Christian, he wrote what he had in his blood, not the intellect, between impototence and ignorance, with a dazzling, nonsense pometic humor, like the knife blade that was about to kill him."
On Graham Greene: "Our man was abdicated by this woman with a Passion that lasted thirteen years, in whose flesh the excitement of adultery with the pleasure of remorse, a spiritual privilege that consisted of reaching heaven through the path of perdition."
About James Joyce: "El 'Ulises' was published in Paris in 1922 by Sylvia Beach. It is one of the peaks of eight thousand meters of universal literature, which must be scaled through the northern wall, from which the best mountaineers are sprawled again and again."
On William Faulkner: "She was a weird guy.
From himself, he sometimes said that he was the heir to a county landlord and others that he was the son of a black woman and a crocodile.
Both dreams were of grandeur."
About Louis-Ferdinand Céline: "This writer picked up the demented cry thrown from a bridge by that Munich character to bring his echo to the bottom of the 20th-century night in his literary form and did so on a journey fleeing from himself and invoking posterity with a violent speech to worms."
About Dorothy Parker: "One day he got on his knees and prayed: 'Dear God, I beg you to stop writing like a woman.'
About Joseph Conrad: "About his tomb were engraved these Spenser verses: 'Sleeping after the effort,/ after the storm the port,/ the rest after the war,/ after life fed up it pleases death."
About Virginia Wolf: "In luggage he also brought his depressions.
Hussband would normally accept that she told her that Edward VII spied on her among the azaleas or that the birds sang in Greek.
There has never been the case of a man so patient and in love with a neurotic whose literary talent was ahead of his madness."
About Pío Baroja: "What did Martín-Santos do but to try to inoculate Joyce in Baroja?
What did Benet's try but to pass Baroja through Faulkner's weapons?
What did Cela do but abduct the fame of that man to serve as his own pedestal?"
Co-degree assault
Last week, my 70-year-old mother was walking through our neighborhood in the municipality of Fuenlabrada when a group of young people between the ages of 15 and 18 passed next to her and our dog, a mestizo-bred specimen, rescued from the kennel and with no more than six kilos of weight and, without a word, kicked two kicks that left the dog badly injured.
Our indignation is capital because we didn't find the fun in a gratuitous assault on a small and helpless animal, which, by the way, was stuck.
To this we must add the suffocation caused to a lady who was walking quietly and that, when he disbelieved these individuals, he came to fear for his physical integrity, since an energity that attacks an animal is capable of doing the same with a woman, a child, an old man or, in short, with anyone who is weaker than himself.
The event occurred at five o'clock in the afternoon of any Tuesday through a traditionally quiet neighborhood.
The dog was crying all day.
By the way, we filed a complaint at a nearby precinct that we doubt will serve a lot and not to generate susceptibilities, only to clarify that the coward killers were Spaniards.
The indignation has led us to denouncing this fact.
We don't understand that it's happening among young people so they'll think it's fun to mistreat a helpless animal free of charge that gives us affection, company and friendship.
We don't know where good education and respect for animals and people have stayed.
Michelin and Fesvial together for the wear of helmet
The Michelin tire manufacturer, with the collaboration of the Spanish Foundation for Road Safety (Fesvial), has launched a campaign to promote the use of the helmet, mainly among younger motorists, both entities reported today.
This initiative seeks to raise awareness of the importance of using the helmet, since it is the only protective element capable of avoiding head injuries or even death in the event of an accident while riding a motorcycle.
Michelin pointed out that this campaign is part of its commitment to road safety, which "goes beyond designing and manufacturing increasingly safer products" and stated that it also contributes to this goal through other pedagogical and informative actions.
This new campaign to promote helmet wear on the motorcycle, under the motto 'To be not to be', will have a first phase in which posters will be distributed in more than 500 motorcycle workshops, with the aim of achieving the maximum dissemination.
Finally, Michelin emphasized that road safety "is a constant concern" for the company, since being a manufacturer of two-wheel-drive tires, one of its main aims is to develop increasingly safe products.
The sale of light commercials rises
Almost two years later, the light-changing gadget market begins to see some glimpse at the end-of-strengthen.
The 9,425 units that were registered in November in Spain represent an increase of 12.6% compared to 2008 and, more importantly, represent the first increase after 22 consecutive months of decreases, according to figures from the employers of the manufacturers Anfac and that of sellers Ganvam.
It should be quarantined, the good data, should be quarantined since the reference with which the comparison is made - November 2008 - was particularly bad, with a decrease of 60% compared to the previous year.
As a result, despite the rebound in the last month, the enrolments accumulated in these 11 months are 40% below those of the previous financial year.
Since January 95,853 units have been sold together all the vehicles that make up the tailor's drawer of the light commercials: derivatives of passenger cars, pick-ups, vans, light vans and light trucks/chasis.
In addition, the clouds that most affect their demand have not disappeared, because although they are also acquired by individuals, most purchases are made by small and medium-sized enterprises, which pay in almost 100 per cent of cases through external financing.
So to the restrictions imposed by the closed tap of bank credits, there must be added other factors such as the increase in levels of unemployment or the persistence of the poor economic situation.
Faced with this scenario and unlike passenger cars, aid for the purchase of 2000E has been of little use.
In addition to individuals, the self-employed and SMEs that will acquire a light commercial of up to 3.5 tonnes with a CO2 emission level not exceeding 160 grams per kilometre cannot be used, but the number of operations has been testimonial.
Yesterday from Ganvam they again remembered the need to devote special attention from the Administration to these vehicles and also to industrialists (trucks and buses).
The sellers' association forecasts a 2010 similar to the end year, for which it calculates a drop in sales (of cars and 4x4) of 19%.
Emergency braking aid is already mandatory
As was the case with the ABS anti-bllock and will go through ESP stability control, emergency braking support systems will have to be a mandatory element in European cars.
In fact, it is already in all cars and light commercial vehicles of new registration, while for the rest a period of deficiency is set until the end of February 2011.
The measure, imposed by the European Union, aims to increase pedestrian protection even though, because of their way of working, it can also help to avoid many collisions by scope.
The assistant to the emergency brake what it does is to increase the pressure on the brakes in the event of an emergency, which the system detects through the trambling given by the driver.
But it doesn't always maintain that pressure until the end.
According to a study carried out by car component maker Bosch, one-third of the drivers involved in an accident had failed to step on the brake before the collision and half of them did not use the full force.
Up to 1,100 accidents
The intervention of the aid, on the other hand, requires the maximum to the braking system, reducing the distance used by the car to stop.
According to a study by the EU itself, if all the cars were equipped with this type of element, up to 1,100 fatal accidents involving pedestrians could be avoided each year.
The reduction will become even greater - it is estimated that one in four sinisters with damage to people would be avoided - when the so-so-so-so-called intelligent emergency braking system is popularized.
In this case, the vehicle is equipped with a system that (through a radar or camera) detects the obstacles and warns the driver, in addition to acting lightly on the brakes.
If the driver reacts, it helps him by increasing the pedal's pressure, if necessary.
In the event that it does not react, and although the collision is inevitable, the device exerts the maximum effort on the brakes to minimize the damage.
