At the wheel of the Porsche Boxster Spyder
In order to develop their last, and face jewel, Porsche engineers took the Boxster S as its base and managed to thin none less than 80 kilos, which has left the scale at only 1,275 pounds.
This led them to dispense, in the first place, of the automatic roof that has been supplied by one canvas with manual drive, thus saving 21 kilos; using aluminum doors such as GT3, 'falling' another 15; removing the air conditioner, 13; reducing the fuel tank from 64 to 54 liters, they earned 7 more kilos; riding sports bacquets another 12 and with light tires of 19 inches, five.
