CNMV Authorizes Paternina Exclusive Opa presented by Ininvestra Mer
The National Securities Market Commission (CNMV) yesterday authorized Exclusion opa presented by Ininvestra Mer on Federico Paternina on October 9.
The supervisory body has explained that it authorizes this operation on the understanding that its terms are in accordance with the current rules and to consider "sufficient" the content of the explanatory brochure presented following the amendments introduced on 2 December.
The CNMV has specified that the offer is aimed at the acquisition of 550,008 shares of Federico Paternina at a price of 7.65 euros per share, which represents 8.95% of its share capital, which consists of 6,144,786 shares admitted to trading on the Stock Exchanges of Madrid and Bilbao.
He also explained that 5,592,778 million shares have been immobilized, which cannot be transmitted in any way until the conclusion of the offer, of which he has specified that the price has been fixed by Federico Paternina, in accordance with the provisions of the current regulations.
New Tools to Persecute Cars
In these days of storms and accidents, not only do car workshops gain.
Every day thousands of cars that have suffered a sinister are towed to a workshop, where an expert must evaluate the damage suffered and what will be the cost of repair.
No sinister is the same, and the calculus of the costs of pieces and the time of labor can be a long and complicated task.
Calculate the cost of a repair of between 20,000 to 30,000 euros, including yman pieces of construction, it can take two or three hours.
On the other hand, with the support of the most recent computer tools it would be a matter of minutes
That's why almost 100 per cent of experts use these types of systems.
Service providers and solutions for proprietary and maintenance are dedicated to collecting the information provided to them by the manufacturers, and then preparing it and offering it to their customers in the form of a useful tool.
In Spain, Audatex, of the American group Solera, is the leading firm; 80% of the valuations are made with its products.
The other firms that compete in the field of valuation and information-processing tools on the sector are GtMotive and Eurotax.
Working with the data provided by the manufacturers is far from simple.
According to Eduardo Velázquez, commercial director of Audatex, in Spain they work with 63 manufacturers and importers, and each of them provides them with the information in different formats.
In addition, the amount of data to be processed continues to increase, to the extent that in the last five years more versions, variants and motorizations have been released than in the previous fifteen.
As soon as a new car gets on the market, these companies get to work.
It is a very arduous task, because you have to catalogue each of the thousands of parts of the vehicle and introduce its price.
In addition, of each model a "smart" graphic image is made where you can "puncture" different parts of tourism.
If it's a sales model, the work can be ready within a week if the process goes very quickly.
If it is a minority car, it can take three or four months. Currently, Audatex has complete information about 99.2% of the cars that are marketed in Spain.
Among the most exclusive models they have information about Porsche, but not of Ferrari or Lamborghini, for example.
As for the mobile park circulating, they exceed 99 per cent.
To carry out the work of documentation and the elaboration of the databases, Audatex has eight centers distributed around the world (Spain, France, Germany, the United States, Brazil, Mexico, China and Japan), and each of them specializes in specific brands.
The national headquarters is in Alcobendas (Madrid).
There, more than a hundred technicians (unusually expert in mechanics) work simultaneously with three computer screens.
Audatex invests EUR 90 million per year to produce these databases.
Every month 2.5 million data is included, and customers receive updates every two days.
The elaboration of this enormous flow of information allows these companies to give them different uses and offer varied products.
The most common use focuses on repair and maintenance, but according to which countries there are also tools for the management of scrapping parts or to calculate the venal or residual value of a car.
The only company that has a guide that informs about the value of those used in Spain is Eurotax.
Audatex doesn't offer it in our country, but in the U.S.
In view of the products offered by Audatex it is easy to gain an idea of the type of support they can provide to professionals in the sector.
This company offers ten different tools, being the AudaPlus star product, the standard disaster valuation solution, intended for the experts.
Excludes cars, motorbikes and light or heavy commercial vehicles.
In addition to the cost of the parts, it includes the repair times estimated by the manufacturer (s).
This tool is repaid according to the use, for every valuation.
The highest cost is 5.75 euros, for customers who wear it little, a maximum of ten times a month.
Then each insurer, which performs thousands of experts, negotiates its price with Audatex.
Other products, such as AudaVIN, allow the total identification of a vehicle and the equipment with which it came out of the assembly line only with its rack number.
AudaGlass is concentrated in the moons of the vehicles, and AudaSubastas is a service open to the professional sector on the Internet that allows to bid for vehicles declared total sinister.
Its statistical service is very useful to identify trends, perform geodemographic analyses, or know deviations from omodel marks.
You can study, for example, how many models of a particular brand have gone through the workshop because of breakdowns or how many have suffered serious casualties over a certain period.
Gt Motive is the only Spanish company dedicated to the development of these types of tools.
It commercializes, among others, Gt Estimate, which is also destined for experts and also provides digital images, access to parts or prices and official times of the manufacturer.
Gt Motive is an Einsa group company founded in 1971 as a service provider and damage-proacity valuation, breakdowns or automotive maintenance
The Gt Appliance Guide is its historical reference product on the market.
They work with 24,000 users in workshops, 3,100 experts and 53 insurance companies.
Its turnover has grown at a rate of 20 per cent a year over the past three years, and in 2008 they billed 10.8 million euros.
At the beginning of last year they began their process of internationalization with the installation of an office in Paris.
For its part, Audatex was born in Germany in 1966 and in 1979 was established in Spain.
According to the company's sources, 62 per cent of its business is generated in Europe and the rest of the world, and the remaining 38% in North and South America. They work with 900 insurance companies and 33,000 workshops, 3,000 of them in Spain.
The global turnover of the Solera group (Audatex, Sidexa, Informex ABZ, Hollander and IMS) will reach 557 million dollars, 3.3% more than in 2008.
In our country the company will enter 19.1 million euros, 7.2% more than the previous year.
In 2005, the Solera group was worth $1 billion on the Stock Exchange, and its shares are now listed for a total value of $2.4 billion.
Since 2007 it has been listed on the New York Stock Exchange and is included in the benchmark Standard & Poor's index.
Internet upstairs of rugged cars
Last October the Solera group bought Autoonline, an internet platform for the sale of cars such as motorbikes or sinister special vehicles.
The operation resulted in a disbursement of EUR 59.5 million for 85 per cent of the company &apos; s capital, which could be extended next year to the remaining 15 per cent.
The objective of the acquisition was to offer more value-added services to its customers, with the possibility of accessing an immense international market.
This valuation and sale service is aimed exclusively at professionals in the sector, such as insurer companies, experts, renting companies, workshops, scrappers and professional sellers who must register before starting to carry out operations.
This platform was created in 1996 in Germany and manages more than 650,000 operations throughout Europe, 500,000 of them in Germany.
Its main markets include Spain, Greece, Poland and Turkey.
The website currently has more than 1,500 registered sellers and 4,000 experts.
3,000 advertisements a day are managed and about 100 new advertisements are included in the Spanish market every day.
According to the Spanish law, a car whose rack number has been decommissioned cannot re-route, but certain undamaged dishes can be used as a replacement.
The cars with historical value can be discharged even if they have been decommissioned after far-wrong efforts.
Quarter-to-eight workshop budget
With the Auda-Taller tool, the Audatex company guarantees that the user obtains a budget in just four steps: to identify the vehicle, to look for replacement, to create budget and to generate budget.
Easy to use is an essential determinant for these systems, especially to convince older professionals, who to a greater or lesser extent are usually more reluctant to use new management techniques.
The database includes 1,034 vehicles, including 666 cars, 109 SUVs, 137 motorcycles, 78 vans and 44 lorries.
Naturally, to use it requires a computer with internet connection.
. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
Users can include variables such as labor price, surcharges or discounts, and can then print the budget to deliver to the customer.
AudaTaller isn't a valuation tool like AudaPlus, but rather a catalogue of references.
The main difference between the two systems is that workshop oriented doesn't include estimated workload times.
The cost of using this tool for the workshop is 350 euros a year, which the client can finance.
Audatex is currently working to make these images three-dimensional.
This is an innovation that mechanics see with very nice eyes, as it will allow, for example, to select a door and turn it around to see the inner face.
